`sha256d` occurs 0 times in it). No extracted link is claimed anywhere below.

Section 2 states the domain and the exclusions the composition inherits, including the
2^61-byte padding-domain limit, with a checked counterexample at the limit.

Section 3 is the class-level obstruction: every map built from `+`, `ringMul sigma` and
constant points over `Apeiron.Trichotomy.AnyRing` preserves the congruence read at the ideal
generated by `2^j`, for every `j` and - the point of it - for every `sigma`, since `sigma`
never enters the argument. Section 4 instantiates it at the three named faces.

Section 5 localises the obstruction to the two bit-moving primitives `rotr` and `shrx`, with
numeral witnesses at the canonical 32-bit width. Section 6 is the iteration verdict: the four
